<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Radio Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Radio Luxembourg was a commercial radio station broadcasting from the Grand Duchy from 1933, run by the Compagnie Luxembourgeoise de Radiodiffusion. Its powerful transmitters reached audiences across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and its English-language service, outside the BBC's monopoly, became famous for popular music and youth programmes from the 1950s. The company that ran it grew into the broadcasting group RTL.</p></div>
